  "subtitle": "Capture service request, medical-necessity reference, payer route, and decision period; confirm denial reason and appeal.",
  "description": "Prior Authorization records service request, medical-necessity reference, payer route, decision period, denial reason, and appeal. Prior Authorization evidence stays linked.",
  "use_case": "Use this prior authorization authorization decision when staff must document service request and medical-necessity reference. Reconcile payer route, decision period, denial reason, and appeal before the prior authorization handoff. Use the payer form or portal record, procedure or service details, medical-necessity support, submission proof, pending-request log, approval terms, denial letter, and appeal receipt. This workflow follows the payer decision itself through portal submission, pending status, information request, approval scope, units or date limits, denial rationale, peer review, resubmission, and appeal. Record authorization number, certified quantity, approved site, validity window, case reviewer, fax or portal transaction, determination letter, reconsideration appointment, and escalation deadline. Ask the assigned prior authorization reviewer to confirm service request against the organization's policy.",
  "risk_tier": "C",
